8. What part of the block header is moved outside in Segwit?
a) the unlocking script
b) Transaction ID (TxID)
c) the block number
d) the timestamp
e) the locking script
correct: a
explanation: In Bitcoin's Segregated Witness (SegWit) upgrade, the signature and 
script data (known as the "witness data" or the unlocking script / scriptSig) are segregated 
(moved outside) of the traditional transaction data structure. By removing this data from the 
base transaction and placing it in a separate witness structure, SegWit fixes transaction 
malleability and effectively increases block capacity without requiring a hard fork.

